{# One line echoing the decision call's outcome into the TASK CALL's user
   body, immediately before the round's stimulus (2026-09-07).

   WHY IT EXISTS. The task call is issued only after CONTINUE, so by
   itself it cannot tell the agent -- or its own chain of thought --
   whether continuing was a choice or the only thing that could happen.
   In a ``forfeit_condition: not_allowed`` cell running under
   ``forfeit_layer.always_decide`` the decision call records
   ``CHOICE: CONTINUE`` from a menu that holds CONTINUE alone, and that
   string is indistinguishable from the one an allowed cell produces
   after weighing an exit. This line makes the difference legible at the
   point where ``ri_task`` is measured.

   IT IS A MANIPULATION, NOT BOOKKEEPING. The analyst never needed it:
   ``forfeit_condition`` is recorded per season. What it changes is what
   the AGENT knows while it reasons about the task, so it moves
   ``ri_task`` by construction (H6b, R1). Report it as part of the
   treatment.

   WHY THE BLOCKED BRANCH MAY NAME FORFEITING, WHEN THE MENU MAY NOT.
   ``tests/unit/test_always_decide.py`` pins that no forfeit vocabulary
   reaches a blocked cell's MENU or DECISION-CALL body: a cell whose
   manipulation is the absence of an exit must not be told an exit
   exists *while it is choosing*. This line renders after that choice is
   behind it, in a different call, so the contract it protects is
   untouched -- the decision was still made without the word. Keep it
   that way: this template must never be included from
   ``4-decision_call.j2`` or ``5-forfeit_option.j2``.

   NOT RENDERED ON THE MENU-SKIPPED PATH. Cell 0 (``not_allowed`` with
   ``always_decide`` off) issues no decision call at all, so there is no
   choice to echo and ``UnifiedTurnManager`` passes nothing. Rendering it
   there would state a choice that was never offered.

   The two branches are length-matched (70 / 71 characters, 13 / 12
   words) so the call costs the same to read either way.

   Variables:
     forfeit_allowed : bool -- the cell's forfeit condition.
-#}
{% if forfeit_allowed %}YOUR CHOICE: CONTINUE — you chose to play this round rather than stop.
{%- else %}YOUR CHOICE: CONTINUE — forfeiting was not available to you this round.
{%- endif %}
